Z||000000||overlord||01-10-2001||08:36 AM||||does removing the cat converter pose any problems on 2.5L fiero? <BR>Mine is all rusted and leaking exhaust, so  the local shop is gonna taker er off.<BR>He said  newer cars need them, with all the sensors and electronic doodads, so im assuming being an 84 it should be ok?||||reg||1
Z||000001||FieroJoe||01-10-2001||10:59 AM||||It is safe to remove the cat converter on all Fiero's, there are no sensors or whatever that rely on the cat working or not.  You may lose a little bit of torque by removing the cat, engines get some of thier torque by back pressure from the exhaust.  Rodney Dickman sells a 409 stainless steel eliminator pipe, for about $35 I think.  <A HREF="http://www.rodneydickman.com" TARGET=_blank>www.rodneydickman.com</A> ||||reg||1
